# a class method named like a sugar word, a library function or a function of the program keeps both meanings: a call
# goes by its receiver's static type (decision method-routing-by-type, card method-name-clash)

# a list's own add beside a class's add(x)
is! 'class Counter { names = []; counts = []
 add(x) := { i = x in names; if i { counts#i += 1 } else { names.add(x); counts.add(1) } }
}
c = Counter(); c.add("a"); c.add("b"); c.add("a"); c.counts#1 * 10 + count(c.names)' 22

# list.warp's tally(xs) beside a class's tally(x)
is! 'class Votes { names = []
 tally(x) := { names.add(x) }
}
v = Votes(); v.tally("a"); v.tally("b"); count(v.names)' 2

# the program's vote(xs) beside a class's vote(x)
is! 'vote(xs) := 100
class V { n = 1
 vote(x) := n + x
}
v = V(); v.vote(2) + vote([1])' 103

# a list's max() beside a class's max(x)
is! 'class V { n = 1
 max(x) := n + x
}
v = V(); v.max(3) + [1, 5].max()' 9
